$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A: Suzuki Coupling I. General Procedure
for the Synthesis of 1b, 1f and 1g .
2-Bromo-4-cyanobenzaldehyde/2-bromobenzaldehyde/3-bromothiophene-2-carbaldehyde
(10 mmol), phenylboronic acid/benzo[b]thien-3-ylboronic acid (11 mmol),
K2CO3 (20 mmol), PPh3 (20% mol), Pd(OAc)2 (10% mol) were placed in a 25
mL Schlenk flask, which was flushed with argon prior to use. Then 16 mL
of 1:1 v/v mixture of toluene and water was added, and the resulting
mixture was stirred at 80 °C for 16 h. Then 15 mL of water was added, and
resulting mixture was stirred for another 15 min. Two phases were
separated, water phase was extracted with toluene (3 × 10 mL). Organic
phases were combined and dried, solvent was evaporated and crude products
were purified by means of flash column chromatography.
2-(Benzo[b]thiophen-3-yl)benzaldehyde (1f). Yellow oil. Yield 1.67 g
(70%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.87 (s, 1H), 8.10 (dd, J 7.9, 1.1 Hz,
1H), 7.96-7.93 (m, 1H), 7.69 (dt, J 7.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.58-7.54 (m, 1H),
7.54-7.50 (m, 2H), 7.43-7.35 (m, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 191.9,
140.0, 139.34, 139.30, 134.9, 133.9, 133.4, 131.3, 128.4, 127.6, 126.4,
124.9, 122.85, 122.69. HRMS (EI) calcd for C15H10OS 238.0452 [M+], found
238.0459.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM χ-Shaped Bis(areno)-1,4-dihydropyrrolo[3,2-b]pyrroles Generated by
Oxidative Aromatic Coupling
